    "chunk_text": "\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f \u0bc6\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0bae\u0ba4\u0baf\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bc6 \u0b95\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0b95\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb5\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b8e\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b95\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0ba3\u0baf\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1 \u0b85\u0bb1\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0bae\u0b95 \u0ba4\u0baf\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd \u0baa\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bc7\u0ba9 \u0b8e\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0ba4\u0bc1. (a) (i) A three-year plan had been prepared for rice\n\nand additional food crops from 2027 to 2029.\n\nA plan up to 2040 has not been prepared.\n\n1. Programme for Enhancing Local Dairy\n\nProduction (Dairy Hub) - Rs. 1,000 million\n\nThis programme is implemented with the aim of uplifting dairy farmers and making Sri Lanka 75 per cent self-sufficient in milk by the year 2030.\n\n2. Programme for Improving Breeding\n\nUnits at Several Farms Belonging to the National Livestock Development Board - Rs. 1,000 million\n\n(ii) An annual forecast plan has been prepared\n\nto reduce food imports. According to the Organizational Result-based Framework developed from 2025 to 2029, its baseline year is 2024.\n\n(iii) The following tasks are planned to be carried out from 2027 to 2030 for this purpose:\n\n\u0b86\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1 \u0b8f\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0bc7\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0ba4\u0bc6\u0baf\u0bcd\u0ba4 \u0b85\u0bb3\u0bb5\u0bc1 (\u0ba4\u0bc7. \u0ba4\u0b9f\u0bc6\u0bbe.)\n\n2021 2,736\n\n2022 7,488\n\n2023 2,189\n\n2024 173\n\n2025 4,249\n\n1. In order to accelerate agricultural\n\nmechanization in the country, plans are underway to establish approximately 200 Agricultural Machinery Hubs Island-wide, through which farmers can obtain quality services on a rental basis at the required time. It is expected to spend about Rs. 2,000 million for this purpose.\n\n2. It is expected to spend approximately\n\n20 million rupees to train about 2,000 skilled operators to operate agricultural machinery.\n\n3. It is expected to spend Rs. 20 million\n\nto conduct awareness workshops on the proper maintenance and functioning of agricultural machinery.\n\n4. Approximately 500 million rupees is\n\nexpected to be spent on research in the field of agricultural mechanization and for promoting new machinery among farming community.\n\n\u2022 Approximately Rs. 100 million is"
