    "chunk_text": "this time. Predicting the specific year in which Sri Lanka will substantially eliminate the importation of major food crops in order to conserve foreign exchange is challenging due to various factors including changes in agricultural policies, climatic conditions, technological advancements and economic developments. Based on medium-term\n\n981 982\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0d9a\u0dca.\u0da9\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0dbd\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dc1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dc1]\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0db4\u0dba\u0dd2 05\n\nAccording to production data from the past 10 years, among the field crops cultivated in Sri Lanka, the domestic production of sesame, groundnuts, red onions, cowpea and green gram fulfils more than 50 per cent of their annual requirement. In this regard, the sesame crop has reached a self-sufficient level and sesame exports are also taking place. In addition, measures are being taken to achieve self-sufficiency levels for groundnuts, black gram, red onions, cowpea and green gram as well. However, in respect of crops such as maize, potatoes, big onions and soybeans, a greater proportion of the annual requirement is met through imports than through domestic production. Similarly, a considerable portion of the requirement for maize and black gram is also met domestically.\n\n(*The average value of production for 10 years\n\nfrom 2016 to 2025 has been considered.)\n\nCrop Annual production (MT)*\n\nAnnual Requirement (MT)*\n\nSelf-sufficient Rate (%)\n\nMaize 272,523 700,000 39\n\nPotato 67,462 225,000 30\n\nBig onion 36,013 325,000 11\n\nRed onion 55,767 80,000 70\n\nSoybean 5,769 13,000 44\n\nGreen gram 13,533 25,000 54\n\nCowpea 11,872 18,000 66\n\nBlack gram 9,807 25,000 39\n\nGroundnut 29,129 40,000 73\n\nFinger millet 7,781 10,000 78\n\nSesame 10,466 7,000 150\n\n(vi) Currently, the surplus production of sesame\n\nis exported.\n\n(vii) Since the target markets and projected\n\ntimelines relating to the period 2027-2040 have not yet been prepared, they cannot be presented to this House at this time. (b) The target markets and projected timelines relating to the period 2027-2040 are expected to be prepared in the future."
