    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/23527_english_2026-05-05.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-05-2026-05-05-0248",
    "chunk_index": 248,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "8fe2f635fbd06330346421fdd026cdbd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1828,
    "chunk_text": "(iii) Under the Tourism Act, No. 38 of 2005, officers of the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority and the Tourist Police Division are not vested with powers related to law enforcement such as conducting investigations, recording statements, searching property or persons, making arrests or detentions or imposing on-the-spot fines.\n\nComplaints submitted by tourists are directed to the Tourist Police Division for necessary action.\n\nComplaints relating to registered institutions or individuals are initially addressed amicably or through verbal inquiry by Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority. Where such matters cannot be resolved, it is advised to refer them to the relevant police authorities.\n\nAll complaints that fall under criminal law or the general law are referred to the Tourist Police or, through the Tourist Police, to the relevant police stations.\n\nComplaints regarding the standards and quality of institutions registered under our Authority are referred to the Standards and Quality Assurance Division of the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority for appropriate action.\n\n(iv) Since 29.09.2025 to date, 63 on-site inspections have been conducted on unregistered tourism establishments. Due to the difficulties faced by tourism sector\n\noperators as a result of the impacts of Cyclone \u201cDitwah\u201d, on-site inspections were not carried out for a considerable period. However, necessary steps are now being taken to resume and continue those activities.\n\nNo penalties have been imposed so far, and approval has been obtained from the Board of Management of the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority to initiate legal action against 34 institutions. Final notices have already been issued to them. Legal proceedings will be instituted in the future based on the advice of the Attorney-General's Department."
  },
