    "chunk_text": "Over the past 10 years, the Coconut Development Authority has implemented various research and development programmes with the objective of promoting growth in the coconut and coconut-based products sector, identifying consumption trends and formulating extension strategies in line with modern market requirements.\n\nDuring this period, a scientific and market research was conducted in the following key areas.\n\n\u2022 National-level survey on coconut oil production and consumption\n\n\u2022 Analysis of coconut consumption patterns and household-level usage trends\n\n1025 1026\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0d9a\u0dca.\u0dc0\u0dd3\u0db8. \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dca\u0dad \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dba\u0dc1\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca\u0db1 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dc1]\n\n2026 \u0db8\u0db4\u0dba\u0dd2 05\n\n\u2022 Survey to identify small, medium\n\nand large-scale entities based on coconut oil production capacity\n\n\u2022 Research on the use and market\n\ngrowth of packaged coconut milk and coconut milk powder\n\n\u2022 Provincial-level consumption analysis (coconut, coconut oil, coconut milk, coconut milk powder)\n\nThese research studies have enabled the identification of public food consumption habits, regional variations and emerging market opportunities.\n\n2. Modernization programmes\n\nBased on the research findings, the following modernization measures have been taken:\n\n\u2022 Introducing new products to\n\npromote the use of packaged coconut milk and coconut milk powder.\n\n\u2022 Raising public awareness on the\n\nuse of healthy coconut oil.\n\n\u2022 Promoting value-added coconut\n\nproducts (e.g. coconut milk powder, coconut milk, coconut cream, virgin coconut oil).\n\n\u2022 Introduction of packaging methods to meet new market requirements.\n\n3. Extension programmes\n\nExtension programmes have been implemented among the public and industrialists based on research and modernization outcomes. In particular, priority has been given to implementing programmes aimed at minimizing household coconut waste.\n\n\u2022 Awareness programmes through\n\nsocial media, electronic media and print media\n\n\u2022 Workshops and training programmes at the regional level\n\n\u2022 Trade exhibitions\n\n\u2022 Consumer awareness promotional campaigns\n\n\u2022 Awareness programmes within"
