    "chunk_text": "\u2022 In 2025, subsidies of Rs. 100,000.00 per person were provided to 23 coconut treacle, coconut jaggery, coconut sugar and coconut ice-cream industries.\n\n\u2022 In 2025, subsidies of Rs. 250,000.00 per person were provided for 18 eco-friendly coconut shell charcoal stoves.\n\n\u2022 Providing assistance for coir\n\n\u2022 Conducting training programmes at\n\ndistrict level.\n\n\u2022 Conducting technology exchange\n\nprogrammes.\n\n\u2022 Providing support for activities\n\nrelated to the establishment of the Coconut Triangle in the Northern Province.\n\n\u2022 Implementing awareness programmes Island-wide to obtain GMP quality certificates. As a result, many industries have already obtained GMP quality certificates.\n\nAccordingly, over the past 10 years, the research, innovation and extension programmes implemented by the Marketing Development and Research Division have made a significant contribution to strengthening the coconut industry on a scientific and market-oriented basis. \u2756 Coconut Research Institute\n\nThe Coconut Research Institute has issued recommendations and conducted research to increase coconut yield and enhance the productivity of coconut cultivation.\n\n1. Genetically improved coconut production\n\n2. Methods to minimize the impacts of climate change on coconut cultivation\n\n3. Methods to be followed to improve soil quality\n\n4. Fertilizer application\n\n5. Research on pest and disease control in coconut cultivation\n\n6. Research on the production of value-added products in the coconut industry\n\n7. Research on the health benefits of coconut products\n\n8. Research to support policy decision-making in the coconut sector\n\n9. Collection of all data related to the coconut sector\n\n10. Analytical services required by\n\nstakeholders and customers in the coconut industry\n\n11. Maintenance of seed gardens for the\n\nproduction of hybrid and high-quality coconut seeds\n\n12. Establishment and supervision of\n\ncoconut seed gardens for hybrid seed production in collaboration with the private sector\n\n13. Certification of coconut seedlings"
